    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1939357108769550708",
      "url": "https://x.com/RareRestore/status/1939357108769550708",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/RareRestore/status/1939357108769550708",
      "text": "give me solutions rare, not problems - ok, fine, here's what i'd do if i'm Ronin r/n:\n\nimo, price is down only without new users\nso primary focus is UA, secondary focus is games \n\n1) ignore anything that isn't gaming\n\nto be king of the gaming chains, it has to be this way\n\n2) group games into casual, degen/casino/gamba, and everything else\n\nthis helps with targeting our new users \n\n3) facilitate sharing (links > creator codes)\n\nprovide all games with an out of the box referral system that uses links, not creator codes (Tribally has this)\n\n4) show meaningful support to Ronin builders -tweeting 'look at the price of this NFT collection' does nothing, Ronin games need to be front & centre of ad campaigns \n\nexample 1: video\n\n- create promo content (3 genres to get you going - casual, degen/casino/gamba, everything else)\n- leverage sth like Sploot from @jonahblake so you have a wealth of footage\n- spend on ad placements where gamer traffic is high (YouTube, TikTok & in-game would be my starting point, then moving to streamers) \n\nside note:\ni'd pause all spend on creators who have no reach outside of CT (300 creators producing 15000 pieces of content in 7 days just spams the TL and does nothing for UA)\n\nexample 2: written/blog/advertorial \n\n- leverage AI to turn threads from the likes of @0xnathan into long form articles and distribute on sites with high gamer traffic\n- incentivise long form content (manual at first, then automated)\n\nexample 3: physical\n\n- Ronin x Jolibee / McDonalds is easy, but not cheap\n- put a mascot (the @SkyMavisHQ Bird? @Ronin_Network's Jin on a Ship? @RonkeOnRon?) into kids happy meals\n- this could be part of a longer term play where kids become familiar with Ronin IP over time, but i'd be doing more here and making sure the toys have a QR code so that kids can claim a playable (and onchain) version of the toy they just got\n- give those kids a frictionless way to play their new character in sth like Axie DoLL (Ronin Wallet lite?)\n\nexample 4: education\n\n- partner with someone like @bitskwela, who focus on blockchain education in Filipino schools\n- this is a longer term strategy but when we did this there were short term benefits, including a nice users spike and a front page feature on a national newspaper in the Philippines \n\n5) no more onchain games\n\n- most of them are terrible and have token baggage\n- onboard offchain indie studies to Ronin\n- they will like the super cheap UA\n- let them lean on web3 elements as needed\n- (you know Tribally has this tech)\n- onchain interactions are good for $RON (minting of e.g. achievements, daily streaks, player archetypes) \n- all players transact in $RON \n\ndisclaimer:\n- this is a mind dump with no prior planning",
